y - Electrical Outlets Covered: An outlet was accessible to younger children in care in a classroom.  This was immediately corrected when an outlet cover was placed over the exposed outlet.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026491187","violation_type_title":"Safety - Electrical Outlets Covered (26 TAC §746.3701(1))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-8","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205","date":"2025-02-05","original_code":"746.3407(8)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-02-07","finding":"Garbage Inaccessible to Children; Maintained in Sanitary Manner: Trash cans utilized by younger children in care did not have lids making trash accessible to children in care.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026250625","violation_type_title":"Garbage Inaccessible to Children; Maintained in Sanitary Manner (26 TAC §746.3407(8))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5311-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205","date":"2025-02-05","original_code":"746.5311(a)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-02-07","finding":"Smoke-Detection System: Two classrooms utilized by children in care did not have working smoke detectors.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026290638","violation_type_title":"Smoke-Detection System (26 TAC §746.5311(a))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3803-a-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205","date":"2025-02-05","original_code":"746.3803(a)(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-02-07","finding":"Medication Authorization - Signed and Dated: Three children medication records did not have parental signature authorizing medication administration.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026250626","violation_type_title":"Medication Authorization - Signed and Dated (26 TAC §746.3803(a)(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205","date":"2025-02-05","original_code":"746.3701","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2025-02-05","finding":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards: Two shelves in the infant classroom presented a tipping hazard should the infants in care pull-up on the shelving.  The infants in care had access to the shelves as the shelves had toys on them for the infants in care.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026371445","violation_type_title":"Safety - Areas Free From Hazards (26 TAC §746.3701)","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3701-9","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20250205","date":"2025-02-05","original_code":"746.3701(9)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Safety - Bodies of Water Inaccessible to Children: A large plastic tub of standing gray water was observed under a sink in the bathroom utilized by children in care.  The washer back flowed into the children's sink in the bathroom, causing concern that the children in care had access to contaminated gray water in conjunction with standing water.  This was immediately corrected during the inspection when the tub of water was emptied and the children in care no longer had access to the bathroom temporarily.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026290637","violation_type_title":"Safety - Bodies of Water Inaccessible to Children (26 TAC §746.3701(9))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1453906-i20240814","dat